stream + 7 unchanged P1a tests, and 8 Node + 8 actual Chromium P1b cases, including the corrected removal control. No skips or absent required cases were accepted. I inspected both actual future-exclusion traces: each reports the retained-member active/decrypted control and removedFromGroup at epoch 1 versus remaining epoch 2 with direct cryptographic decryption failure.\nRuntime: Node 26.8.1, Chromium 153.0.8010.12 revision 1243, macOS arm64. The application build/Worker dry run remains unbound and undeployed; real browser crypto execution does not add a Worker crypto claim.\n\nRetained independent evidence under /Users/hughpyle/play/noseq-worktrees/ordered-mls-probe:\n- artifacts/harness/5c31e2f8-1306-4e8d-9f00-8bcdf2546387/evidence.json, SHA-256 d33827281c02125c00a46394d6b34ed9c7a5c0a8c2c8bfabe9206b3358b8adf0.\n- artifacts/crypto-preflight/runs/d3083349-4566-45ae-b636-e56f5c7ecf5c/evidence.json, SHA-256 e8b2a251ec8d66ee05ed33d900f4fbfdfc2de76537eba0f11836373155b9e94f.\n- artifacts/ordered-mls/runs/bdb0f20d-b52b-4d0e-9692-1377bea0c77c/evidence.json, SHA-256 f65bc8962d02161e646bae6affbd63efaef8adefa109fd03a3a5a3d237538ac1. The Node/browser future-exclusion observations and all raw process/test reports are retained in that run.\n- artifacts/ordered-mls/reviewer-fix-verification/f3149df2-efc3-4ace-8608-5bdb32f28d5d/summary.json, SHA-256 6e134203813807fdf4dad4392f36fefc720c153313e4c927f73b6b05fcb5aeb9. Nine expected public CLI outcomes matched: the valid record passed; missing removal case, missing removal observation, corrupted observation, false G1 claim, failed browser process, and prior-source evidence each failed; test:crypto-feasibility and gate:protocol both remained nonzero.\nThe unchanged verifier's wider 24-outcome negative review remains recorded in #290; the focused new checks confirm current-source binding and corrected-case evidence. The earlier dirty-source failure and both independent experiments exposing P1B-01 remain present and unmodified.\n\nPrimary-source basis is unchanged from #290: the actual pinned implementation and RFC 9750 section 5.2.1 / RFC 9420 section 14 motivate the bounded ordered-self-echo/Welcome investigation, without substituting for full application security evidence:\nhttps://github.com/hzrd149/ts-mls/tree/2ca5c43b77241245ef41a5dd834f151674877c2d\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9750.html#section-5.2.1\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9420.html#section-14\n\nReady for requester ratification and guarded landing of this bounded development investigation. All G1-G5 remain unpassed; production adoption requires its own future reviewed and ratified decision.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:3694d7bff36cc98c6d65ab51d5a5305f004cb588","head":"5a8a45d76922399b41141a97baab100dfadbdff9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:288edb044a435660d4936675aaa55d8652a8d01c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:288edb044a435660d4936675aaa55d8652a8d01c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}